r sense than that of 'autumnal'.\n\nTerms: तत्-पुरुष समास", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["शारदेअनार्तवे ६.२.९", "६.२.९", "६.२.९ शारदेअनार्तवे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["SAradeanArtave ६.२.९", "६.२.९", "६.२.९ SAradeanArtave"]}], "sarvan guRakartsnye": [{"id": "sarvaM guRakArtsnye", "headword": "सर्वं गुणकार्त्स्न्ये", "headword_slp1": "sarvaM guRakArtsnye", "fold": "sarvan guRakartsnye", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The acute accent (उदात्त) is on the final of the word सर्व standing as the first member before an attributive word in the sense 'whole, through and through'.\n\nTerms: समास end acute-1st-term", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सर्वं गुणकार्त्स्न्ये ६.२.९३", "६.२.९३", "६.२.९३ सर्वं गुणकार्त्स्न्ये"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sarvaM guRakArtsnye ६.२.९३", "६.२.९३", "६.२.९३ sarvaM guRakArtsnye"]}], "saradinan ca": [{"id": "SarAdInAM ca", "headword": "शरादीनां च", "headword_slp1": "SarAdInAM ca", "fold": "saradinan ca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The final vowel of शर etc. is lengthened before मत् when it is a name.\n\nTerms: संहिता Lengthening", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["शरादीनां च ६.३.१२०", "६.३.१२०", "६.३.१२० शरादीनां च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["SarAdInAM ca ६.३.१२०", "६.३.१२०", "६.३.१२० SarAdInAM ca"]}], "sarvanamasTane casambudDO": [{"id": "sarvanAmasTAne cAsambudDO", "headword": "सर्वनामस्थाने चासम्बुद्धौ", "headword_slp1": "sarvanAmasTAne cAsambudDO", "fold": "sarvanamasTane casambudDO", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In a अङ्ग (stem) ending in न् the preceding vowel is lengthened in strong cases with the exception of the Vocative Case singular.\n\nTerms: Lengthening", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सर्वनामस्थाने चासम्बुद्धौ ६.४.८", "६.४.८", "६.४.८ सर्वनामस्थाने चासम्बुद्धौ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sarvanAmasTAne cAsambudDO ६.४.८", "६.४.८", "६.४.८ sarvanAmasTAne cAsambudDO"]}